erdict."},{"consequence":"informs","id":"effects_unavailable","kind":"partial_input","reason":"effects_unavailable","severity":"info","sourceRecords":["review.effects"],"summary":"Change effects (new calls, side effects, reachability) were not analyzed for this change."}],"evaluatedRevision":{"baseSha":"bc02c7ca0ccb25adda074262202c99cd7b89a536","evaluatedCommit":"cd52be1ef12c062c90e14b1101db64a91c392725","headSha":"5e0d6f332a34408d66c4108ea3dbbea5d16c1ec4","mergeBaseSha":"bc02c7ca0ccb25adda074262202c99cd7b89a536","policyDigest":"sha256:41821244536b349aa3071da362373be36d68f2af2b1423495b1e8d70612f221f","policyRevision":"bc02c7ca0ccb25adda074262202c99cd7b89a536","producerRunId":"run-361ec70a1760d6956ea5872b862665f6425d93bea4d2b4d4b5366248c5f8418b","treeKind":"synthetic_merge"},"intendedChange":{"changedRequirements":[{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","title":"Unparseable input (after stripping), non-object JSON, and non-object entries yield an empty or skipped item set; no exception escapes the parser. Trailing-comma stripping is string-aware. It preserves commas inside string literals verbatim. It drops only a comma outside any string whose next non-whitespace character is } or ] (trailing_comma_dropped = !comma_in_string && next_char_closes_json)."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260927-66FW","title":"When the JSONC stripper sees a comma, it drops the comma only when the comma sits outside each string literal. The next non-whitespace character after the comma must be a closing brace or bracket. A comma inside a string literal is data and stays unchanged."},{"changeStatus":"added","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260928-BMFE","title":"A top-level JSON array is not an object map of menu entries. The parser returns an empty item set for it, as it does for every other non-object root. No phantom rows with numeric ids appear."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","title":"The default JSONC and the user extension merge into one ordered item tree: per-key user overrides, stable order, inferred kinds and parents, injected root."}],"linkedIssues":["#13492","omacom/omarchy#13492"],"sources":["changeRequest.body","changeRequest.linkedIssues","changeRequest.title","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","requirement:SW-REQ-260927-66FW","requirement:SW-REQ-260928-BMFE","requirement:SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"status":"declared","title":"Fix menu JSONC top-level array rendering phantom rows"},"nextDecision":{"disclosureIds":["policy_changed_unclassified"],"kind":"human_judgement","question":"Should the 1 protection reduction this change makes be accepted under the prior approved policy?","reason":"protection_weakened"},"preservedBehaviour":{"requirements":[{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"The rewrite touches only the plain $(reader) form, mapping it to the captured slot. command -v reader, VAR=x reader, and every other form runs the real command."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"An entry with action is an action, with target a link, otherwise a menu. An undeclared parent derives from the dotted id (or root). Root's parent is empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-74BZ","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A route matching no id and no alias resolves to the literal input. A misspelling still attempts to open that id without a rewrite."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A user entry overrides the default per key while keeping the row's original order slot. The model injects a root item with label Go when no source declares one."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Absent an exact id, a route equal to a declared alias resolves to the id of the item declaring the alias. Alias comparison lowercases and maps underscores to dashes."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A row matches only when every query term appears in its name text (label, leaf id, aliases) or as a whole word in its description. Invisible and disabled rows never match."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","matchLevel":"function","relation":"code_changed","title":"The parser strips full-line // comments and trailing commas before JSON parsing, so the authored JSONC parses to its declared entries."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"swapProviderRows drops exactly the rows carrying the re-run provider's providerMenu and appends the new batch, leaving static children and other providers' rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Applied guard results drive the view. A row hides when its when: is false. A static submenu or link hides when no descendant is visible, while provider-backed menus stay visible. A checked:true or disabled:true row earns the check-mark label. A disabled row dims and skips the cursor."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-MQ37","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"The generated guard script holds exactly one if-line per declared when, checked, or disabled, each echoing <id>:<w|c|d>:<0|1>; items with no guard get none."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-N3RM","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When a route resolves to an action item with a non-empty action, the action runs directly and no menu opens."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-PRNV","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"An exact id match wins over every alias. App rows are never routable, so an installed app's keywords cannot shadow a menu route (htop ships Keywords=system)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-RGCV","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"relation":"code_changed","title":"The prelude's omarchy-pkg-present/missing shadows agree with pacman -Q everywhere. This covers provides resolution, version constraints deferred to pacman, and the no-argument case (present true of nothing, missing not)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Scores tier exact label, whole-word app name, label prefix, label substring, name text, then description. Menus and links promote by 2, apps demote by 5 within a tier. Final order breaks ties by depth then declaration order."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Search lists current-menu matches before deeper (drilldown) matches, with a divider section exactly when both groups are non-empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-W17G","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A value command shared by several guards (e.g. omarchy-default-browser across seven rows) runs once per batch, captured eagerly before any guard line."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-XW52","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When a route resolves to a link item, the menu opens at the link's target."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Y58B","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When no item declares a guard, the guard script is empty and no guard process runs."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z680","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"mergeAppRows and swapProviderRows return fresh maps that drop orphan ids and the replaced batch. They list a duplicated incoming id once and never write into their input maps."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Dynamic rows (apps, provider enumerations) replace their source's previous batch atomically: orphans dropped, duplicates listed once, static rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A route string (exact id, declared alias, or normalized spelling) opens the item it denotes; unknown strings fall through as literal ids."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A filter query narrows to visible, selectable rows whose name or description matches every term, ranked by match quality."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260927-WC89","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee engages the session lock and exits 0. This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu."}],"total":23},"readiness":"blocked","readinessBasis":"introduced","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:41821244536b349aa3071da362373be36d68f2af2b1423495b1e8d70612f221f","policyRevision":"bc02c7ca0ccb25adda074262202c99cd7b89a536","requiresPriorPolicySignoff":true,"role":"policy_approver"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":0,"gatesAdvisory":26,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":170,"testsPassed":0},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbol` / line ranges (authored + derived) and function-local annotations; a whole-file trace is file-level (weak) and says nothing about which function a requirement needs.","Intent relations: requirement level = satisfies/parent or siblings under a parent with <= 20 children; component level = shared component (incl. traces.components); contract level = an interface requirement naming both components. A missing spec edge can make a real dependency look uncodified, and a broad contract